  "title": "Integer Linear Forms for a Factorial Reciprocal Series",
  "subject": "Erdős #68",
  "subject_kind": "problem",
  "form": "Problem note",
  "pages": 9,
  "question": "Which integer coefficient vectors cancel initial weighted sums in factorial-denominator linear forms?",
  "precis": "For S=∑_{n≥2}(n!−1)^{-1}, the paper classifies finitely supported integer vectors that cancel prescribed initial weighted sums in forms MS+k. An integral basis, one Diophantine equation and a finite gcd determine the possible moments M. At cancellation depth four, the least positive moment is 1380. Irrationality by these forms still requires a nonintegral form with q dividing M for every positive q.",
  "owns": "the coefficient classification, finite moment gcd and depth-four construction; the long paper develops denominator exclusions, further constructions and method limits",
  "not_authority_for": "the validity of claims tagged Lean, which belongs to the cited kernel-checked source, or a solution to Erdős #68, which remains open",
